+# Agent Note: Composition settings with local credentials
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-14-composition-settings-with-local-credentials.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+Assisted enterprise enrollment needs DSH's native credential entry without allowing a stored settings section to redirect that credential to another API endpoint. The Models onboarding joins provider and settings descriptors with the independent credential service. Removing settings prevents that join; retaining a writable settings file lets user values override composition defaults.
+
+## Decision
+
+The [composition-only settings provider](../../../../packages/settings/settings-file/src/composition-only.ts) is an explicit subpath export. It resolves registered schemas and composition bases over an empty user document, reports settings as read-only, and exposes no local document. It reads, watches and writes no settings file. The shared settings service refuses merge, replacement and path-mutation requests before persistence. The default file-backed export retains its behavior.
+
+The native credential provider remains separate. Its dedicated Key can be entered and persisted while provider settings remain read-only. A deployment must pin the model and search endpoints and credential reference in its admitted composition; this provider alone does not restrict registered bases or network destinations. Installation integrity and trusted plugin resolution remain the Launcher's responsibility.
+
+First-run readiness checks the effective credential's write capability rather than the unrelated settings document's write capability. The credential-only dialog never mutates provider settings. When the welcome section is explicitly ready but read-only, an explicit acknowledgement lasts only for that browser process; a new process must acknowledge again. Missing or failed settings reads do not silently become acknowledgements.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Restore the ordinary writable settings file.** Rejected because endpoint and credential-reference overrides would remain effective regardless of which controls the UI hides.
+
+**Disable settings altogether.** Rejected because native onboarding needs registered settings descriptors to find the configured provider and its credential reference.
+
+**Wait for backend Key delivery.** Deferred for the assisted pilot: administrator-controlled local entry avoids that delivery dependency without routing model traffic through Ensou.
+
+## Consequences
+
+The provider prevents user settings documents from changing the composition's values, including across restart, but does not protect against code running as the same OS user. Native credentials remain file-backed, not encrypted by this provider. It does not revoke a Key at DeepSeek Platform or enforce employee identity.
+
+The [Loader and credential tests](../../../../packages/settings/settings-file/tests/composition-only.spec.ts) verify read-only settings rejection, absence of settings-file effects, disposal, and synthetic credential persistence across reconstruction with an unrelated entry preserved. The [onboarding component regression](../../../../packages/client/ui-settings-models/tests/onboarding-dialog.client.spec.tsx) verifies native credential-only save without settings mutation; [welcome regressions](../../../../packages/client/ui-settings-models/tests/welcome-store.client.spec.ts) retain explicit acknowledgement and durable-write error behavior. The full Models editor currently treats read-only settings as a read-only editor, so later Key editing through that page is not provided by this change. Published CLI, browser interaction and real-provider acceptance remain separate verification work.
