+# Agent Note: Trusted client module discovery
+
+Status: implemented
+
+English | [中文](2026-09-14-trusted-client-module-discovery.zh.md)
+
+## Problem
+
+A managed Host imports plugins through an installation-owned resolution table. Client discovery repeated ordinary resolution from the CLI root, which does not directly depend on every bundle-owned client package. The actual built browser received an empty graph and could not preload its module kernel, even though Host boot passed. Both managed profiles reproduced this failure.
+
+## Decision
+
+[Client Modules](../../../../packages/client/modules/src/index.ts) consumes the exact Host-verified resolution for each bare package when the trusted service exists. It checks the physical installation and package boundaries, manifest name and anchor; a missing or inconsistent entry fails without an ordinary-resolution fallback. Loader builtins remain excluded. Ordinary, untrusted-mode discovery keeps its existing resolver.
+
+## Alternatives considered
+
+**Add every client package to CLI dependencies.** Rejected because bundle ownership already declares those relationships, and duplicating the roster would drift on upstream updates.
+
+**Ignore the failed resolver and return an empty graph.** Rejected because a listening Host is not evidence of a usable browser.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Host imports and the browser graph now use the same installation identity. The dependency on app-boot is type-only; the module package does not mint trusted tables. Regression tests cover trusted discovery and refusal paths, and managed boot tests must check a nonempty graph with its kernel bootstrap entry. Built-browser interaction, installed-client update/recovery and production admission remain separate acceptance layers.
