+## Managed runtime replacement
+
+The Launcher-authenticated `enterprise-direct-local` profile and an explicitly opted-in Personal `web` profile accept the private `ensou.dsh.runtime-update.v1` named-pipe lifecycle. Drain first stops Web admission, synchronously fences every new or live Agent at its real maintenance boundary, then waits credential and settings queues plus every live Session durability listener. A missing or failed durability participant restores admission and reports `resumed`; only a complete checkpoint reports `ready`, after which the exact operation may request graceful whole-tree shutdown. Ordinary profile launches without the exact inherited bootstrap are unchanged.
+
